  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "o1XhmbjxKgiYj9t2rgtlB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 183.29291464979684,
      "y": -72.57195281982422,
      "width": 1031.3431396484375,
      "height": 1180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1861917925,
      "version": 3365,
      "versionNonce": 1052140229,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795062162923,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional : \nusers shouldbe able to generate a short url by logging in to the website or thru api, paste their url and should generate a short url\nUsers when visit this short url should be navigated to the original url\nUsers, should also be able to generate their own, if it's taken then we generate a random one\nExpiry, user can set an expiry date, links without one never expire, when users vists an expired link show link expired\nAnalytics, clicks per link would be nice\nSame url shortened multiple times should generate same code\n\nNon funtional requirements : \nSCALE\n  Writes: 100M/month ≈ 40/s avg, ~120/s peak\n  Reads:  10B/month  ≈ 4,000/s avg, ~12,000/s peak   (100:1, read-heavy)\n  Storage: 6B links × ~500 B ≈ 3 TB over 5 years\n\n8 core cpu, each core about 1000/sec, thats' about 10000/sec, so i would add 2\none load balancer\ncache, most asked codes, cache at cdn for users closest to the region\none write replica, as 120/sec is something it can handle easily\n2 read replicas, with strong consistency\n\nLATENCY\n  Redirect p99 < 100 ms (global) · Create < 1 s\n\nAVAILABILITY > CONSISTENCY\n  Redirects must stay up; seconds of staleness OK\n  Codes must be unique (strong at create time only)\n\nGEOGRAPHY\n  Global users → edge/CDN + multi-region reads\n\n\nReturn 302 for everything for control and analytics, front door caches with a short ttl\n\n\nAPI Contracts\npost/ generateShortUrl\nRequest : string longUrl, string shortUrl = null, dateTime expiryDate = null\nResponse : string shortUrl\n\nget| getShortUrl\nqueryString : string shortUrl\nResponse : {string shortUrl, string longUrl, uniqueId}\n\nredirectService\nget / code\npublish an event\nthen redirect to long url\n\n\n\nLinks\nid = 7 digit code itself\nlongUrl = string\nownerId \nexpiryDate \ncreatedAt\nupdatedAt\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional : \nusers shouldbe able to generate a short url by logging in to the website or thru api, paste their url and should generate a short url\nUsers when visit this short url should be navigated to the original url\nUsers, should also be able to generate their own, if it's taken then we generate a random one\nExpiry, user can set an expiry date, links without one never expire, when users vists an expired link show link expired\nAnalytics, clicks per link would be nice\nSame url shortened multiple times should generate same code\n\nNon funtional requirements : \nSCALE\n  Writes: 100M/month ≈ 40/s avg, ~120/s peak\n  Reads:  10B/month  ≈ 4,000/s avg, ~12,000/s peak   (100:1, read-heavy)\n  Storage: 6B links × ~500 B ≈ 3 TB over 5 years\n\n8 core cpu, each core about 1000/sec, thats' about 10000/sec, so i would add 2\none load balancer\ncache, most asked codes, cache at cdn for users closest to the region\none write replica, as 120/sec is something it can handle easily\n2 read replicas, with strong consistency\n\nLATENCY\n  Redirect p99 < 100 ms (global) · Create < 1 s\n\nAVAILABILITY > CONSISTENCY\n  Redirects must stay up; seconds of staleness OK\n  Codes must be unique (strong at create time only)\n\nGEOGRAPHY\n  Global users → edge/CDN + multi-region reads\n\n\nReturn 302 for everything for control and analytics, front door caches with a short ttl\n\n\nAPI Contracts\npost/ generateShortUrl\nRequest : string longUrl, string shortUrl = null, dateTime expiryDate = null\nResponse : string shortUrl\n\nget| getShortUrl\nqueryString : string shortUrl\nResponse : {string shortUrl, string longUrl, uniqueId}\n\nredirectService\nget / code\npublish an event\nthen redirect to long url\n\n\n\nLinks\nid = 7 digit code itself\nlongUrl = string\nownerId \nexpiryDate \ncreatedAt\nupdatedAt\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
